      "text": "\n\n<think>\nThe user wants me to write an incident retrospective for a production API outage caused by a bad cache invalidation rule. Let me structure this carefully with all the required sections: impact, timeline, contributing factors, detection gaps, remediation, prevention work, and owner handoff. It needs to be 450-550 words, practical language for engineers and managers, concise but complete.\n\nLet me think about what makes a good incident retrospective:\n- Blameless tone\n- Specific technical details that make it feel real\n- Clear timeline\n- Actionable items with owners\n- Not overly formal but professional\n- Practical language - not corporate fluff\n\nLet me draft this:\n\nTitle: Incident Retrospective \u2013 API Outage (Cache Invalidation Rule)\n\nI'll structure it with clear headers and keep the language direct. Let me aim for around 500 words.\n\nLet me write it out and count words carefully.\n\n---\n\n**Incident Retrospective: Production API Outage \u2013 Bad Cache Invalidation Rule**\n**Date:** 2025-06-14 | **Severity:** SEV-1 | **Duration:** 47 min\n\n**Impact**\nBetween 09:12 and 09:59 UTC, the /v2/orders and /v2/inventory endpoints returned 503s for ~34% of traffic. Downstream effects: checkout page showed stale prices, the mobile app's \"add to cart\" flow failed for ~12,000 sessions, and the ops dashboard went dark for 11 minutes. No data loss. Estimated revenue impact: ~$18K in abandoned carts.\n\n**Timeline (UTC)**\n- 09:02 \u2013 Deploy #4821 ships a new cache-invalidation rule: \"purge all keys matching `inv:*` on any write to `orders:*`.\" Intended to fix a 200 ms staleness window.\n- 09:12 \u2013 First 503s appear. The rule triggers a full-namespace purge on every order write. Under peak traffic (~4,200 writes/min), the cache layer (Memcached cluster, 6 nodes) enters a thundering-herd loop: every miss re-populates, every write re-purges.\n- 09:18 \u2013 PagerDuty fires. On-call (J",
      "text_preview": "\n\n<think>\nThe user wants me to write an incident retrospective for a production API outage caused by a bad cache invalidation rule. Let me structure this carefully with all the required sections: impact, timeline, contributing factors, detection gaps, remediation, prevention work, and owner handoff. It needs to be 450-",
